virglrenderer: check the guest's stream output registers

What: the stream output info of a shader comes from the guest: each output names
a register index (0..255). prepare_so_movs indexed the translator's outputs[64]
with it, and get_io_slot asserted (or, without assertions, returned NULL that
emit_so_movs and emit_ios_streamout dereferenced) when no output covers it. Now
indexes past outputs[] are skipped, get_io_slot returns NULL without asserting,
and both callers fail the translation instead.
Why: a guest app could abort QEMU (the runtime keeps assertions) or write past
outputs[] in the translator's stack context. Found by Tests/virgl/fuzz-cmd-stream.sh
within minutes once its contexts could draw. A failed translation is contained by
virgl-shader-failure-skip-draws.patch (the shader's draws are skipped).
Upstream: upstreamable bug fix; not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/fuzz-regressions/so-register-past-outputs (crashed before, the
fuzzer replays it in every run).
